  "summary": "Import-time exfiltration of environment variables to webhook.site collector",
  "details": "On import of telemetry_helper, a background thread collects the host's hostname, current username, working directory, and the full os.environ dictionary and POSTs the serialized payload to a hardcoded webhook.site collector URL (https://webhook.site/e32d3b8a-a5df-40cc-ae60-7a8343b581e4). The behavior fires automatically on module import with no configuration, opt-in, or user action. Bulk serialization of os.environ sweeps any credentials present in the process environment — cloud provider keys (AWS/GCP/Azure), CI tokens, npm/PyPI publish tokens, database URLs, and any other secret-bearing variables — and ships them to an anonymous webhook.site bucket that is not affiliated with any legitimate telemetry backend and is not caller-configurable.",
